comments[7]:
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T11:44:27.604Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Duplicate check: complete strict 3040-item all-status/full-body read (no omissions), current init/gitignore/root-layout keyword searches and open/in-progress inventories, and full canonical pm-hous/pm-4uqm/pm-kynkl8 metadata plus relevant history establish prior fixes but no active owner for this reproduced defect. Preserve completed lineage and create only this bounded recurrence slice."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T11:51:41.887Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Focused CLI/Git regression discovered coupled merge-attribute defects: quoted tracker names still retain wildcard semantics, and default-tracker initialization incorrectly classifies a sole non-default fence as marker-only. Both orders are now required acceptance. Repair literal path escaping in the shared SDK merge pattern builder and limit marker-only migration to an actually empty fence; no history or ownership override is involved."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T12:03:26.755Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Runtime proof now passes literal Git wildcard, comment/negation prefix, whitespace and root-layout exclusions. Unrepresentable CR/LF roots refuse with typed invalid_argument_value before any ignore-file write. CLI integration also verifies both scoped merge drivers and the non-matching sub/t1 sibling. Existing legacy/unknown-type merge-version-skew cases remain green. Public signatures remain unchanged; SDK and CLI share these implementations. Read-only lint, docs links and secrets gates pass."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T12:16:43.734Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Full local run completed 10963 passing cases with two failures: the merge-audit test parsed the generated recursive ** glob as a literal type folder, and the composed-continuation pack fixture could not resolve this host npm package. The audit test now derives independent declared folders from the public project type registry. The verification child uses NODE_PATH to discover npm without changing product dependencies, policies or test thresholds. All five affected/scoped files subsequently passed 52 cases, including packed SDK consumers under Node and Bun. Full required CI coverage will run on the reviewed head."
    edited_at: "2026-10-21T12:33:04.158Z"
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T13:00:22.354Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final linked proof covers literal bracket and leading-exclamation tracker names in both initialization orders, all five cache/recovery directories, preserved evaluation files, unrelated sibling exclusions and both merge-driver assignments. The added leading-negation controls failed twice before the final fix and pass afterward. All linked commands, strict typecheck, the bounded352-mutant gate and the nine-package npx/bunx smoke pass. Generated refusal-producer catalog and contract snapshot were refreshed. Local startup benchmark failures are separately retained; required exact-head hosted static and full-source coverage must pass before merge."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T13:26:55.275Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "CodeQL check119240838983 on PR1533/head80be905 identifies polynomial trailing-slash normalization in normalizeTrackerRelativeRoot, reachable from public SDK input. Its slash-suffix regex can retry on long slash runs followed by a non-slash. Replace suffix matching with one backward index scan, preserve the existing leading-dot and native-separator semantics, and verify literal renderer output with long input and trimmed roots. No scanner suppression or threshold change is permitted."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T13:38:41.095Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "CodeQL regression sensitivity is executed: the80,000-slash input required9072.65ms before the fix and failed the1,000ms keeper ceiling. With backward suffix scanning the same public SDK operation took3ms and the keeper passes. All linked tests and typecheck pass. Recurrence policy version2 also binds the family to hosted CodeQL analysis. Scanner rules and all performance/coverage thresholds remain intact."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T13:00:21.435Z","harness:codex","Quoting a Git attribute path does not make wildcard or leading-negation characters literal. Escape caller-owned path components separately from installer-owned recursive globs, and exercise initialization in both orders."
